<i>Lancet</i>2009 (RCT, n=2, 246 children; no increase in post-extubation stridor with cuffed tubes). Maintain cuff pressure ≤20 cmH₂O. Have one size smaller available.</td></tr></table><div class="sh p">RSI Drugs — Pediatric Weight-Based Dosing</div><p style="font-size:0.71rem;color:#555;text-align:center;margin-bottom:9px">PALS 2020 · Verify all doses against current guidelines and local formulary · Broselow tape recommended in emergency</p><table class="tbl p"><tr><th>Drug</th><th>Pediatric Dose (IV)</th><th>Notes &amp;
Specific Cautions</th></tr><tr><td><b>Ketamine</b></td><td>1–2 mg/kg IV · 4–6 mg/kg IM</td><td><b>Drug of choice</b>for pediatric emergency RSI;
