2 yrs — use with caution;
can rescue CICO if rocuronium used (reversal in ~3 min at 16 mg/kg)</td></tr></table><div class="sh p">Preoxygenation &amp;
Safe Apnoea Times</div><div class="alert p"><b>Pediatric Apnoea Tolerance (Approximate — based on healthy, well-preoxygenated patients)</b><ul style="padding-left:17px;margin-top:7px;line-height:1.95"><li><b>Neonates (term):</b>SpO₂ falls to 85% within <b>60–100 seconds</b>of apnoea (Kennedy et al., Paediatr Anaesth 2019)</li><li><b>Infants 3–12 months:</b>approximately <b>70–100 seconds</b></li><li><b>Children 1–8 yrs:</b>approximately <b>2–4 minutes</b>(improved significantly with HFNO)</li><li><b>Older children &gt;
